<title>INDIA: Indian soybean, oil, meal firm.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean, oil, meal firm.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were firm in central Indian markets on very poor arrivals on Monday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Prices rose by 100-150 rupees per tonne. Most of the markets of central India were shut ahead of the closing of the financial year. Business volumes were dull and the undertone was firm.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices remained firm on limited supply against better demand. Selling from plants and refineries was limited and traders were hoping prices might go up further. Business volume was good and the undertone was strong.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were firm on limited selling from Indian processors and exporters. Soymeal yellow was $308-309 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) in bulk for export. Rapeseed extraction was $116-117 per tonne FAS in export and was 4,000-4,050 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition. Business volume was dull but the undertone was strong.</p>
